data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` with `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** It works just like any other unmanaged type:

```csharp
Span<nint> nints = stackalloc nint[5];
Span<nuint> nuints = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

On this 64-bit system, `nint` is 8 bytes and `nuint.MaxValue` is `18446744073709551615` (2⁶⁴−1). No `unsafe` context is needed — the `Span<T>` version of `stackalloc` is safe. The only caveat is that `sizeof(nint)` requires an unsafe context (use `nint.Size` instead in safe code).
